ros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution could result from routine scheduling or seasonal demand. The number of contracts near the limit does not prove violations, as market rates or budget constraints might justify such amounts.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of December contracts to see if they align with other contracts. Review awardee A's contracts to determine if they repeat the same service or need. Look at contract [1] to confirm if the amount is consistent with market rates for the service provided.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["1kyBF8ZnzMeopEMYCmrbmw%3D%3D","SYkqROzbOKrua%2Fi14w%2FPLA%3D%3D","YqTJ1scrzs8Xhk1FZxEyvw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}